# ArduPlane Parameters - GPS Failure EKF Glitch Radius 10 Envelope
# Apply after config/vehicles/plane_base.parm and config/overlays/plane_gps.parm.
#
# Purpose: envelope comparison for GPS failure behavior. This lowers
# EK3_GLITCH_RAD from the 25 m baseline to 10 m, the bottom of the parameter's
# documented @Range (10 100), while leaving the innovation gates at their
# baseline values. It is not the default GPS failure overlay.
#
# Any non-zero radius keeps the reject-and-reset path reachable, unlike the
# ekf_gate300_glitch0 envelope where GLITCH_RAD=0 selects the clip-and-fuse
# branch and makes reset unreachable. The expected trade here is more frequent
# resets, each of smaller magnitude: after every reset the filter reseeds
# position variance to sq(0.5 * EK3_GLITCH_RAD) per axis, so the absolute
# headroom to the next reset falls with the square of the radius.

EK3_GLITCH_RAD 10
